# <Platform> Tracker

**Purpose:** Running performance record for one platform. Copy this template to `.work.biz/pipeline/<platform>-tracker.md` (for example `substack-tracker.md`, `threads-tracker.md`, `youtube-tracker.md`) the first time you publish there.

**Why per-platform files rather than one big table:** each platform's meaningful metrics differ, and a shared schema forces you to track impressions everywhere, which is the metric least connected to revenue. Keep `reference/CONTENT_STATUS.md` as the cross-platform index of what exists; keep this file as the per-platform performance record.

**Last updated:** <date>

---

## Channel status

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Role in channel plan** | `primary` / `supporting` / `secondary` / **`not sanctioned`** |
| **Sanctioned in `strategy/channel-plan.md`?** | yes / no — if **no**, stop and resolve the drift before publishing more |
| **Committed cadence** | <e.g. 1 long-form/week> |
| **Actual cadence, last 4 weeks** | <count> |
| **Started** | <date> |
| **Expected time to inbound** | <e.g. 6-12 months for authority channels> |
| **Weekly hours cost** | <real number, including the engagement window> |

**Drift rule:** if actual cadence is under half the committed cadence for three consecutive weeks, this channel is not being run. Either cut it or cut something else. Record the decision in `context/HANDOFF.md` rather than letting it decay silently.

